<header><p class="enc-kicker">Person</p><h1 class="enc-title">Hermann von Salza</h1><p class="enc-meta"><span class="dates">c. 1165–1239</span> · <a href="/centuries/13th-century">13th century</a></p></header>
<div class="enc-body"><p class="enc-desc">Hermann von Salza was Grand Master of the <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/teutonic-order">Teutonic Order</a> from 1210 to 1239. A trusted adviser of Emperor <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/frederick-ii">Frederick II</a> who also mediated between the emperor and the <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/papacy">papacy</a>, he obtained the <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/golden-bull-of-rimini">Golden Bull of Rimini</a> and papal grants that founded the Order's state in <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/kingdom-of-prussia">Prussia</a>. Under him the Order grew from a small hospital brotherhood into a major military order.</p><figure class="enc-fig"><img src="/images/encyclopedia/hermann-von-salza.jpg" alt="Hermann von Salza" width="320" height="457" fetchpriority="high"><figcaption>Image: Public domain · <a href="https://commons.wikimedia.org/wiki/File:Hermann_von_Salza1.jpg" target="_blank" rel="noopener">Wikimedia Commons</a></figcaption></figure></div>
